<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Bhadrawah State</h1><p class="st-meta">1400 CE – 1846 CE (approx.) · capital Bhadrawah</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small hill state in a high valley off the Chenab, contested by Chamba and Jammu before it became part of Jammu and Kashmir.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhadarwah">Bhadrawah</a> was ruled by local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> chiefs; tradition dates the state to around 1400, but its early history is poorly recorded.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Set in a green upland valley, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhadarwah">Bhadrawah</a> was for long periods a tributary or dependency of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chamba-state">Chamba State</a>. Its people spoke Bhadarwahi, and its Vasuki Nag temple is an important local shrine. Little detail of its government survives.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhadarwah">Bhadrawah</a> passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulab-singh">Gulab Singh of Jammu</a> and became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/jammu-and-kashmir-princely-state">Jammu and Kashmir (princely state)</a> in 1846. It is now a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doda-district">Doda district</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/bhadrawah-state.jpg" alt="Bhadrawah State" width="320" height="180"><figcaption>Image: Manjeet singh · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhaderwahi_folk.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1400 CE – 1846 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bhadrawah</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bhadarwahi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bhadarwah</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1623&amp;focus=bhadrawah-state" aria-label="Bhadrawah State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6620 980 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bhadrawah State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6940 1236L6954 1250"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6954 1250h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6940 1236h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6940 1236h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1623&amp;focus=bhadrawah-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

